  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f$ be a real valued continuous function defined on the positive real axis such that $g(x)=\\int_0^x \\mathrm{t} f(\\mathrm{t}) \\mathrm{dt}$. If $\\mathrm{g}\\left(x^3\\right)=x^6+x^7$, then value of $\\sum_{r=1}^{15} f\\left(\\mathrm{r}^3\\right)$ is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "mMkfA",
      "text": "$270$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "zNhEQ",
      "text": "$340$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "rzR0i",
      "text": "$320$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "aP1s3",
      "text": "$310$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$g(x)=x^2+x^{7 / 3}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & g^{\\prime}(x)=2 x+\\frac{7}{3} x^{4 / 3} \\\\ & f(x)=\\frac{g^{\\prime}(x)}{x} \\\\ & f(x)=2+\\frac{7}{3} x^{1 / 3} \\\\ & f\\left(r^3\\right)=2+\\frac{7}{3} r \\\\ & \\sum_{r=1}^{15}\\left(2+\\frac{7}{3} r\\right)=2(15)+\\frac{7}{3}\\left(\\frac{15(16)}{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}$\n$=310$",
    "image": null
  },
